# Shell scripts are served raw to macOS/Linux (curl | bash), where a CRLF
# line ending is a syntax error. Store them as LF whatever the checkout does.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Files this repo GENERATES. Every generator here writes plain 
, and with
# core.autocrlf=true git hands the worktree CRLF - so the moment one of them runs, git
# reports the file as modified with an EMPTY diff and the release gate refuses to cut a
# version ("main checkout is dirty"), which is a stop nobody can act on because there is
# nothing to commit. Declaring them eol=lf, so the worktree matches what the generator
# writes, is what keeps the working tree clean by itself.
*.svg text eol=lf
src/shared/settingsIndex.ts text eol=lf
